.TH CSTRING_AT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_at \- return the character at a given index
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

char cstring_at(cstr s, size_t idx);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function returns the character at the zero-based index that you give.
It returns '\e0' when idx is out of the bounds, and it does not assert.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s     String to query
idx   Zero-based character index
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The character at idx, or '\e0' if idx >= length
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_c_str (3),
.BR cstring_length (3)
